Two things I preserved deliberately rather than idiomatizing:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
- The min/max ternaries are kept as explicit [38;5;10mif a < b { a } else { b }[0m instead of [38;5;10mf32::min[0m/[38;5;10mf32::max[0m. Those Rust methods are NaN-suppressing (they return the non-NaN operand), whereas the C ternary lets a false comparison fall through to the second operand. With NaN inputs the two differ, so [38;5;10mf32::min[0m would have silently "fixed" the behavior.[0m[0m
- The [38;5;10mdelta == 0.0 || max == 0.0[0m early return and the subsequent branch order are left exactly as written, including the negative-zero and NaN paths, where [38;5;10ms[0m/[38;5;10mh[0m stay 0 and [38;5;10mv[0m carries whatever [38;5;10mmax[0m ended up as.[0m[0m
